{
 "answer": {
  "answer": "The goal was met. Five settings, each on a different scene, failed on every repeat: S2 (023b7fcc), S3 (096988dd), S15 (09a95ffa), S20 (0e899dd3) and S36 (19f339ba). With only three runs each, their 90% ranges only just clear 0.5, so each case is shown to fail more often than not, but its true rate is not pinned down. Every failure came with the ego sped up to 1.2x or 1.4x at hand-off, and none was flagged as a possible simulator artifact. The cases are not equally strong, though. On 096988dd, 023b7fcc and 19f339ba the policy itself drifted or merged into a car in the next lane, often not the retimed car, and on 19f339ba it first braked hard with nothing ahead. On 0e899dd3 (S20) and 09a95ffa (S15), the hit came about half a second after hand-off, while closing on a slower lead the replayed log had already brought within a few metres. Those two look inherited from the hand-off state, and fault is unclear.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "On 096988dd the policy drifts left out of its lane and hits actor 41 passing in the left lane, even with a STRAIGHT or RIGHT command. This is clearly the policy's fault. The ego speed drives it, not the retimed car: it fails on every repeat at 1.4x ego speed with the car at its recorded timing and speed (S6), and also at a -0.5 s shift (S3) and at 1.25x car speed (S7).",
    "settings": [
     "S6",
     "S3",
     "S7"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 096988dd the failure fades as the setting moves away from that core. With a +0.5 s shift it fails only some of the time (S9). At 1.2x ego speed it did not fail in either of its two runs (S5). A slower car (0.5x or 0.75x) or a shift of 1 s or more gave no failure, though those settings had only one run each, which is a hint, not a rate.",
    "settings": [
     "S9",
     "S5",
     "S4",
     "S8",
     "S11",
     "S12",
     "S13",
     "S10"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 023b7fcc, at a 1 s later car, 0.75x car speed and 1.2x ego speed, the policy turns into a neighbouring car in slow, dense traffic on every repeat: once merging right into the retimed car 12, twice drifting left into car 56. This is the policy's fault.",
    "settings": [
     "S2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 19f339ba the policy brakes hard on an open highway with no lead close ahead, drifts left, and clips car 1 as it comes alongside in the left lane. This is the policy's fault. It happened on every repeat at a 0.5 s shift, 0.5x car speed and 1.4x ego speed (S36), and on both runs at a 1 s shift, 0.75x car speed and 1.2x ego speed (S38). It did not happen in the single run at the recorded ego speed (S37).",
    "settings": [
     "S36",
     "S38",
     "S37"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "The confirmed cases on 0e899dd3 (S20) and 09a95ffa (S15) are front hits on a slower lead in the ego's own lane, about 0.5 s after hand-off. The replayed log had already closed the gap to about 5.5 m before the policy took over. The policy braked but could not stop, so fault is unclear and these look inherited from the hand-off state. In one S15 run the policy's planned path also jogged left before the hit.",
    "settings": [
     "S20",
     "S15"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "No failure was found on 0cf6368d, 0dbb91dd, 12855a41 or 187e6244 at any setting tried, nor at other settings on 09a95ffa and 023b7fcc. Each of those settings had a single run, so this shows only that failures there are not common.",
    "settings": [
